# Architecture & Product Decisions Log (`docs/DECISIONS.log`)

- **2026-11-23 | Branching & Two-Track Sequencing:** Confirmed executing Track 1 (`feat/helpdesk-assignment`) through full backend/frontend verification first, then branching Track 2 (`feat/ui-redesign`) from `feat/helpdesk-assignment` for the Principal Product Design redesign (Petrol `#0E5A63` + Warm Paper `#FAF9F6`). Never touch `master`, never push, never open PRs.
- **2026-11-23 | Task Assignee Dual-Sync:** Existing `Task.assigned_to_id` references `employees.id` (used by Telegram outbox and legacy tests) while Help Desk & `TeamMember` reference `users.id`. Decision: add `Task.assignee_id` (`users.id`) additively and dual-sync both fields on create/assign so 100% of existing APIs and Telegram integrations remain backward compatible.
- **2026-11-23 | Phase 5 AI Triage Skipped:** Verified `backend/app/api/v1/endpoints/integrations.py` explicitly filters out `gemini` and `backend/requirements.txt` contains no Gemini SDK. Phase 5 AI Triage is skipped per spec ("Only if a Gemini integration already exists in the repo; otherwise skip and report").
- **2026-11-24 | Windows `tzdata` Fallback for Business-Hours SLA:** Python 3.13 on Windows dev lacks the optional `tzdata` wheel for `ZoneInfo("Asia/Riyadh")`. Implemented `resolve_timezone()` in `sla_service.py` trying `ZoneInfo` first (full IANA DST on Linux/Docker) with deterministic UTC+3 / Middle East offset fallback when `tzdata` is absent — zero new dependencies added.
- **2026-11-24 | Notification Priority Safety:** `notification_service.py` calls `email_service.send_password_reset_email(..., raw_token="urgent_alert")` for `priority="Urgent"`. New assignment & SLA escalation services strictly pass `priority="High"` or `"Normal"` (preserving in-app + Telegram outbox delivery without triggering reset emails or touching auth/email code).
- **2026-11-24 | PostgreSQL Migration Verification Scope:** Verified SQLite live round-trip (`upgrade -> downgrade -> upgrade`, preserving 68 tickets, 99 comments -> 99 events, 302 tasks) and reviewed offline PostgreSQL 16 upgrade/downgrade SQL via `alembic --sql`. Live PostgreSQL 16 staging execution remains a pre-prod deployment step.

## 2026-11-24 — Track 2 (`feat/ui-redesign`) Stage 0 & Stage 1 Decisions
- **DEC-UI-001 (WCAG 2.2 AA Calibration on Tertiary Text & Dark On-Primary):** Computed contrast for `#8C877D` on `#FFFFFF` is `3.57:1` (passes WCAG 2.2 AA 3:1 for UI icons/dividers, fails 4.5:1 for normal text). Mapped `#8C877D` to `--icon-muted` and calibrated readable tertiary captions to `--text-3: #6E6960` (`5.32:1` on `#FFFFFF`, `5.05:1` on `#FAF9F6`). Calibrated dark-mode `--on-primary` to `#0A1E20` (`6.98:1` on `#4FB3BC`) because `#FFFFFF` on `#4FB3BC` yields `2.52:1`.
- **DEC-UI-002 (Minimal Dependencies for Primitives & Self-Hosted Fonts):** Proposed `class-variance-authority` (~1.1 KB gzip) and minimal headless Radix primitives (`dialog`, `popover`, `tooltip`, `tabs`) for WCAG 2.2 AA focus-trapping and RTL collision handling, plus self-hosted WOFF2 fonts (`IBM Plex Sans Arabic` + `IBM Plex Sans`, weights `400/500/600`) to remove the external Google Fonts CDN `@import`. Pending Stage 1 user approval.
- **DEC-UI-003 (Frontend Adapters for Backend-Dependent UI Features):** Per strict frontend-only scope on `feat/ui-redesign`, Composer voice clips will reuse existing `POST /api/v1/tickets/voice/upload` via typed `composerVoiceAdapter` (`NEXT_PUBLIC_COMPOSER_VOICE=1`); general non-audio ticket-reply attachments and `/my-work` Snooze will be wired behind typed adapters (`NEXT_PUBLIC_COMPOSER_ATTACHMENTS`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_MYWORK_SNOOZE`) without modifying backend contracts.
- **DEC-UI-004 (Dev Toolkit Overlay Default OFF):** Stage 0 live screenshots proved `<DevToolkitLoader />` occludes sidebar footer controls on desktop and blocks mobile bottom navigation at `390px`. Gating `<DevToolkitLoader />` behind `NEXT_PUBLIC_DEV_TOOLKIT=1` (default OFF) in Phase 4C.
